// Title: UAC Bypass Abusing Winsat Path Parsing - Registry
// Sigma ID: 6597be7b-ac61-4ac8-bef4-d3ec88174853
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Christian Burkard (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-08-30 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, T1548.002
// Description: Detects the pattern of UAC Bypass using a path parsing issue in winsat.exe (UACMe 52)
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/hfiref0x/UACME
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_uac_bypass_winsat.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey contains "\\Root\\InventoryApplicationFile\\winsat.exe|" and RegistryKey endswith "\\LowerCaseLongPath" and RegistryValueData startswith "c:\\users\\" and RegistryValueData endswith "\\appdata\\local\\temp\\system32\\winsat.exe"
